<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Recover the window start for the sittings where it is not a guess (PRD 5.16.1).

      The column arrived with the listening-stretch work, so every row written before it has a
      NULL start and gets no retelling. That was the right default: last_progress_ms minus
      listened_ms is usually the start, but a rewind makes credited time exceed the distance
      covered, and inventing a start is the same class of lie as retelling a book from memory.

      One subset is not a guess, though. When listened_ms EQUALS last_progress_ms, the credit
      counted from zero and nothing was skipped: openingCredit() only hands back the head
      position when the episode was opened within a minute of its start, so equality means the
      sitting ran straight through from the top. For those rows the start is exactly 0, and
      leaving them NULL would withhold a retelling we can honestly produce.

      Everything else keeps its NULL. A sitting that continued yesterday's episode, or that was
      rewound, stays out of the queue until the poller records its start first-hand.
    -->
    <changeSet id="0430-podcast-window-backfill" author="danchuo">
        <sql>
            UPDATE podcast_session
            SET start_progress_ms = 0
            WHERE start_progress_ms IS NULL
              AND listened_ms = last_progress_ms
              AND listened_ms > 0
        </sql>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
